{"module":"environment","voice":"female","duration":179.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Environmental racism: who breathes the dirty air","start":0.0,"end":3.27,"words":[[0.04,1.08],[1.08,1.74],[2.0,2.15],[2.15,2.52],[2.52,2.67],[2.67,2.96],[2.96,3.11]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The same maps that show redlining and urban renewal often show where the landfills, refineries and highways went.","start":4.07,"end":11.97,"words":[[4.12,4.29],[4.29,4.62],[4.62,4.95],[4.95,5.2],[5.2,5.45],[5.45,6.19],[6.19,6.44],[6.44,6.77],[6.77,7.35],[7.35,7.68],[7.68,7.93],[7.93,8.18],[8.18,8.34],[8.34,9.09],[9.38,10.2],[10.2,10.45],[10.45,11.03],[11.03,11.44]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Pollution is another way place decides health and wealth.","start":12.32,"end":15.77,"words":[[12.36,12.85],[12.85,12.99],[12.99,13.33],[13.33,13.54],[13.54,13.89],[13.89,14.38],[14.38,14.66],[14.66,14.87],[14.87,15.21]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Where the movement started","start":16.12,"end":17.7,"words":[[16.17,16.41],[16.41,16.57],[16.57,17.13],[17.13,17.61]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 1982, residents of mostly Black Warren County, North Carolina, lay down in the road to stop trucks carrying soil contaminated with PCBs to a new landfill; more than 500 people were arrested.","start":18.4,"end":32.0,"words":[[18.45,18.59],[18.59,19.59],[19.84,20.49],[20.49,20.63],[20.63,21.13],[21.13,21.42],[21.42,21.78],[21.78,22.28],[22.53,22.75],[22.75,23.47],[23.72,23.93],[23.93,24.22],[24.22,24.36],[24.36,24.51],[24.51,24.79],[24.79,24.94],[24.94,25.22],[25.22,25.58],[25.58,26.08],[26.08,26.37],[26.37,27.3],[27.3,27.52],[27.52,27.95],[27.95,28.09],[28.09,28.23],[28.23,28.45],[28.45,29.02],[29.27,29.42],[29.42,29.63],[29.63,30.42],[30.42,30.78],[30.78,30.92],[30.92,31.5]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 1987 the United Church of Christ's report Toxic Wastes and Race found that race was the strongest predictor of where hazardous waste facilities were located in the U.S.","start":32.35,"end":43.77,"words":[[32.41,32.56],[32.56,33.75],[33.75,33.9],[33.9,34.49],[34.49,34.86],[34.86,35.01],[35.01,35.53],[35.53,35.9],[35.9,36.34],[36.34,36.79],[36.79,37.01],[37.01,37.31],[37.31,37.68],[37.68,37.9],[37.9,38.2],[38.2,38.42],[38.42,38.57],[38.57,39.23],[39.23,39.83],[39.83,39.97],[39.97,40.2],[40.2,40.72],[40.72,41.09],[41.09,41.75],[41.75,41.9],[41.9,42.57],[42.57,42.72],[42.72,42.87],[42.87,43.24]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Cancer Alley","start":44.67,"end":45.88,"words":[[44.67,45.32],[45.32,45.71]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Along about 85 miles of the Mississippi River between Baton Rouge and New Orleans sit well over a hundred petrochemical plants and refineries, many next to Black communities founded by freed people.","start":46.58,"end":59.84,"words":[[46.63,46.94],[46.94,47.33],[47.33,47.95],[47.95,48.34],[48.34,48.49],[48.49,48.65],[48.65,49.26],[49.26,49.57],[49.57,50.04],[50.04,50.42],[50.42,50.66],[50.66,50.89],[50.89,51.12],[51.12,51.58],[51.58,51.82],[51.82,52.05],[52.05,52.36],[52.36,52.51],[52.51,53.05],[53.05,54.06],[54.06,54.52],[54.52,54.76],[54.76,55.61],[55.88,56.19],[56.19,56.57],[56.57,56.73],[56.73,57.04],[57.04,57.81],[57.81,58.35],[58.35,58.58],[58.58,58.89],[58.89,59.36]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In 2014 the EPA estimated that census tracts near the Denka chloroprene plant in LaPlace had among the highest cancer risks from air toxics in the country.","start":60.19,"end":69.88,"words":[[60.24,60.39],[60.39,61.19],[61.19,61.33],[61.33,61.55],[61.55,62.27],[62.27,62.49],[62.49,62.93],[62.93,63.36],[63.36,63.58],[63.58,63.72],[63.72,64.09],[64.09,64.81],[64.81,65.17],[65.17,65.32],[65.32,65.83],[65.83,66.04],[66.04,66.33],[66.33,66.48],[66.48,66.91],[66.91,67.28],[67.28,67.64],[67.64,67.93],[67.93,68.07],[68.07,68.58],[68.58,68.73],[68.73,68.87],[68.87,69.38]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Flint","start":70.78,"end":71.6,"words":[[70.83,71.47]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In April 2014, state-appointed managers switched majority-Black Flint, Michigan, to river water without proper corrosion control, and lead leached into homes for more than a year while officials dismissed residents' complaints.","start":72.3,"end":87.21,"words":[[72.35,72.5],[72.5,72.93],[72.93,73.81],[74.07,75.02],[75.02,75.6],[75.6,76.04],[76.04,76.99],[76.99,77.42],[77.68,78.26],[78.52,78.67],[78.67,78.96],[78.96,79.25],[79.25,79.69],[79.69,80.05],[80.05,80.64],[80.64,81.29],[81.55,81.77],[81.77,81.99],[81.99,82.35],[82.35,82.65],[82.65,83.01],[83.01,83.16],[83.16,83.3],[83.3,83.52],[83.52,83.67],[83.67,83.89],[83.89,84.18],[84.18,84.69],[84.69,85.2],[85.2,85.86],[85.86,86.66]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The Michigan Civil Rights Commission concluded in 2017 that systemic racism played a role.","start":87.56,"end":94.47,"words":[[87.61,87.76],[87.76,88.31],[88.31,88.69],[88.69,89.08],[89.08,89.63],[89.63,90.32],[90.32,90.48],[90.48,91.57],[91.57,91.8],[91.8,92.42],[92.42,93.04],[93.04,93.43],[93.43,93.59],[93.59,93.97]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A settlement of about $626 million was approved in 2021.","start":94.82,"end":100.25,"words":[[94.87,94.99],[94.99,95.57],[95.57,95.69],[95.69,96.01],[96.01,97.74],[97.74,98.12],[98.12,98.31],[98.31,98.69],[98.69,98.82],[98.82,99.84]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Air and heat","start":101.15,"end":102.44,"words":[[101.2,101.49],[101.49,101.92],[101.92,102.35]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A 2019 study in PNAS found that Black and Hispanic Americans breathe more fine-particle pollution than is caused by their own consumption, while white Americans breathe less.","start":103.14,"end":115.36,"words":[[103.2,103.36],[103.36,104.44],[104.44,104.85],[104.85,105.02],[105.02,105.43],[105.43,105.84],[105.84,106.09],[106.09,106.42],[106.42,106.67],[106.67,107.33],[107.33,108.08],[108.08,108.41],[108.41,108.57],[108.57,109.48],[109.48,110.06],[110.06,110.31],[110.31,110.47],[110.47,110.81],[110.81,111.05],[111.05,111.3],[111.3,111.55],[111.55,112.46],[112.75,113.08],[113.08,113.41],[113.41,114.15],[114.15,114.49],[114.49,114.82]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Highways built through Black neighborhoods (see “Burned, flooded and taken”) brought traffic pollution, and formerly redlined areas run hotter in summer (see the module on place).","start":115.71,"end":125.85,"words":[[115.71,116.23],[116.23,116.52],[116.52,116.74],[116.74,117.03],[117.03,117.69],[117.69,117.84],[117.84,118.2],[118.46,118.9],[118.9,119.12],[119.12,119.56],[119.81,120.11],[120.11,120.55],[120.55,121.13],[121.39,121.61],[121.61,122.05],[122.05,122.63],[122.63,123.07],[123.07,123.29],[123.29,123.59],[123.59,123.73],[123.73,124.03],[124.03,124.17],[124.17,124.32],[124.32,124.76],[124.76,124.9],[124.9,125.34]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Intent or economics?","start":126.75,"end":128.48,"words":[[126.8,127.23],[127.23,127.3],[127.3,128.01]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Researchers debate why facilities end up near communities of color.","start":129.18,"end":134.19,"words":[[129.24,129.92],[129.92,130.44],[130.44,130.7],[130.7,131.47],[131.47,131.73],[131.73,131.9],[131.9,132.16],[132.16,133.02],[133.02,133.19],[133.19,133.62]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Some evidence shows they were deliberately placed where residents had the least political power.","start":134.54,"end":139.61,"words":[[134.59,134.79],[134.79,135.23],[135.23,135.49],[135.49,135.68],[135.68,135.81],[135.81,136.52],[136.52,136.9],[136.9,137.09],[137.09,137.67],[137.67,137.86],[137.86,137.99],[137.99,138.25],[138.25,138.82],[138.82,139.14]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Other studies find that, in some places, poorer residents moved in after facilities were built because land and housing became cheap.","start":139.96,"end":148.45,"words":[[140.01,140.23],[140.23,140.68],[140.68,141.06],[141.06,141.36],[141.63,141.78],[141.78,142.0],[142.0,142.61],[142.87,143.25],[143.25,143.93],[143.93,144.23],[144.23,144.38],[144.38,144.68],[144.68,145.36],[145.36,145.51],[145.51,145.81],[145.81,146.19],[146.19,146.49],[146.49,146.72],[146.72,147.17],[147.17,147.62],[147.62,148.0]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Both paths lead to the same unequal exposure.","start":148.8,"end":152.14,"words":[[148.86,149.18],[149.18,149.49],[149.49,149.73],[149.73,149.89],[149.89,150.04],[150.04,150.36],[150.36,150.91],[150.91,151.61]]},{"el":"h5","text":"What helps","start":153.04,"end":154.07,"words":[[153.09,153.4],[153.4,153.92]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Communities have won by organizing, testing their own air and water, and suing.","start":154.77,"end":160.82,"words":[[154.8,155.63],[155.63,155.88],[155.88,156.13],[156.13,156.38],[156.38,157.21],[157.5,158.0],[158.0,158.25],[158.25,158.5],[158.5,158.66],[158.66,158.91],[158.91,159.33],[159.62,159.87],[159.87,160.28]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Federal environmental justice programs expanded under the Justice40 initiative (2021) and were largely rolled back in 2025, so state and local action matters more.","start":161.17,"end":173.79,"words":[[161.18,161.7],[161.7,162.75],[162.75,163.28],[163.28,163.95],[163.95,164.62],[164.62,164.92],[164.92,165.07],[165.07,165.9],[165.9,166.57],[166.57,167.7],[167.96,168.18],[168.18,168.33],[168.33,168.78],[168.78,169.16],[169.16,169.38],[169.38,169.53],[169.53,170.81],[171.07,171.29],[171.29,171.67],[171.67,171.89],[171.89,172.34],[172.34,172.72],[172.72,173.09],[173.09,173.32]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Show up at permit hearings; they are often decided by who attends.","start":174.14,"end":178.34,"words":[[174.16,174.37],[174.37,174.52],[174.52,174.66],[174.66,175.02],[175.02,175.59],[175.84,176.06],[176.06,176.13],[176.13,176.42],[176.42,176.99],[176.99,177.21],[177.21,177.35],[177.35,177.85]]}]}